## Lessons Learned

### Optimize for the Common Case

**Common:** No upstream changes (80% of updates)
**Rare:** Upstream has changes (20% of updates)

Optimizing the common case (skip rebuild) saves 80% of wasted time.

### Flags for Edge Cases

`--force` handles the edge cases:
- First build
- Local changes
- Troubleshooting

Most developers never need it. Power users have it when needed.

### Git as Source of Truth

Instead of tracking "last build time" or "binaries exist," use git:
- `git rev-parse HEAD` vs `git rev-parse origin/main`
- Simple, reliable, no state to manage

If they match → nothing to rebuild.

### Two Commands Is Enough

Resisted adding `install`, `update`, `build`, `rebuild`, `force-rebuild`, etc.

Just:
- `install` - Fresh start
- `update` - Smart incremental
- `update --force` - Edge cases

Simplicity > comprehensiveness.

